WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.975
The rest of the gaps are
about scope and privilege.

2
00:00:02.975 --> 00:00:07.663
To find one app's grants, the script
reads every grant in the tenant.

3
00:00:07.663 --> 00:00:10.518
To review, it signs in
with write permissions,

4
00:00:10.518 --> 00:00:15.149
including the very broad directory
one this chapter is trying to remove.

5
00:00:15.149 --> 00:00:19.163
It names a different administrator
role than the API reference does.

6
00:00:19.163 --> 00:00:21.451
It hard-codes the worldwide host.

7
00:00:21.451 --> 00:00:25.585
And it never looks at directory
roles or Azure role assignments,

8
00:00:25.585 --> 00:00:27.379
so an app in a directory role,

9
00:00:27.379 --> 00:00:32.138
or a managed identity that's Contributor
on a subscription, passes unseen.

10
00:00:32.138 --> 00:00:35.570
So the verdict: use the
requests, not the script.
